  margin-bottom: .5em;
}

table td {
  padding: 0.75em;
}

table tr:hover {
  background: #eee;
}

.year {
  display: table;
}

.month {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-right: 1em;
}

ul {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
}

.nick {
  padding-right: 0.6rem;
  font-weight: bold;
  text-align: right;
  width: 13rem;
  display: table-cell;
}

.nick a {
  color: inherit;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.message {
  display: table-cell;
  padding-left: 0.6rem;
  border-left: 2px solid #333;
}

.notice {
  color: #859900;
  font-style: italic;
}

.line {
  line-height: 1.8rem;
  display: table;
}

#logs {
  margin-top: 1.5rem;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}
</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-10-12.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="002548"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#002548" label="[00:25:48]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">lrvick: hopefully it gets the exposure that you are hoping for.</span></div><div class="line" id="010656"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#010656" label="[01:06:56]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; lrvick: isn't it 256 byte now</span></div><div class="line" id="010658"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#010658" label="[01:06:58]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; not 357</span></div><div class="line" id="010751"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#010751" label="[01:07:51]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; oh, maybe even less</span></div><div class="line" id="010758"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#010758" label="[01:07:58]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; somebody sharnk it to 190</span></div><div class="line" id="010906"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#010906" label="[01:09:06]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">oriansj: have you merged that to stage0-posix-x86?</span></div><div class="line" id="010911"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#010911" label="[01:09:11]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">hmm, possibly no</span></div><div class="line" id="010919"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#010919" label="[01:09:19]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I think hex0.hex0 is out of sync</span></div><div class="line" id="011002"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#011002" label="[01:10:02]">&lt;daddy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I believe we're still on an older version that is 357 bytes.</span></div><div class="line" id="011009"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#011009" label="[01:10:09]">&lt;daddy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">(that's my fault: i have yet to upgrade it)</span></div><div class="line" id="011124"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#011124" label="[01:11:24]">&lt;daddy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">[update?]</span></div><div class="line" id="011238"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#011238" label="[01:12:38]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">anyway, we are also out of sync between bootstrap seeds and stage0-posix-x86</span></div><div class="line" id="011407"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#011407" label="[01:14:07]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">on that PR (<a rel="nofollow" href="https://github.com/oriansj/bootstrap-seeds/pull/44">https://github.com/oriansj/bootstrap-seeds/pull/44</a>)  I've just asked goldstein to update it too. Hopefully they'll be kind enough to do so</span></div><div class="line" id="043342"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#043342" label="[04:33:42]">&lt;Googulator&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it's interesting how both the hex0 POSIX binary and builder-hex0 stage1 converged in 190~192 bytes</span></div><div class="line" id="043352"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#043352" label="[04:33:52]">&lt;Googulator&gt;</a></span><span class="message">*converged on</span></div><div class="line" id="161234"><span class="nick" style="color:#6d2462"><a href="#161234" label="[16:12:34]">&lt;ovf&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Googulator: i see this all the time in code golf. the top solutions will have equal character count and little else in common. i like to think this is some evidence of information theory in action. :-)</span></div><div class="line" id="181148"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#181148" label="[18:11:48]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; Well, this is a bit comparing apples and oranges</span></div><div class="line" id="181213"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#181213" label="[18:12:13]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; POSIX hex0 would have this size with POSIX header</span></div><div class="line" id="181234"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#181234" label="[18:12:34]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; Without header, it is quite a bit smaller</span></div><div class="line" id="181349"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#181349" label="[18:13:49]">&lt;matrix_bridge&gt;</a></span><span class="message">&lt;Andrius Štikonas&gt; Builder-hex0 stage1 is about 200 bytes when looking at just code, with MBR header/footer it is 512 bytes, though largely padding with zeroes</span></div><br /></div></body></html>